{
  "_help": "max_eur = the most this card is worth to you second-hand (EUR). Effective ceiling = min(budget_eur, max_eur). Values are Nov-2026 estimates from eBay sold-price trackers minus ~10% (Cyprus has no buyer protection) - tune them with: python gpu_alert.py --list. Keep the real value even when it is above budget_eur (the ceiling stays at the budget): scam_ratio is measured against max_eur, so a '4090' for 266 is recognised as a fake. The values above 600 are about 10% under the cheapest real used offers on eBay delivered to Cyprus on 2026-11-12.",
  "budget_eur": 600,
  "poll_minutes": 5,
  "great_deal_ratio": 0.8,
  "scam_ratio": 0.4,
  "windows_toast": true,
  "telegram": {
    "bot_token": "",
    "chat_id": ""
  },
  "sources": {
    "bazaraki_pages": 3,
    "vendora_pages": 2,
    "vendora_searches": ["rtx", "radeon", "geforce"]
  },
  "ebay": {
    "_help": "Official eBay Browse API. Runs only after you store your developer keys with: python gpu_alert.py --setup-ebay. Searches Buy It Now listings that ship to deliver_to, newest first, at most budget_eur. price = item + shipping (+ non_eu_import_vat_pct for sellers outside the EU). ceiling_factor multiplies gpus[].max_eur for eBay only: eBay has buyer protection, so 1.1 means paying up to the full used value. Use euro marketplaces only (EBAY_DE, EBAY_IT, EBAY_FR, EBAY_ES, EBAY_NL, EBAY_AT...).",
    "enabled": true,
    "every_minutes": 10,
    "marketplaces": ["EBAY_DE"],
    "deliver_to": "CY",
    "gpu_category": "27386",
    "gpu_searches": [
      "(2060, 3060, 3080, 3090, 4070, 4080, 4090, 5060, 5070, 5080, 5090)",
      "(6700, 6750, 6800, 6900, 6950, 7600, 7700, 7800, 7900, 9060, 9070, a770, b580)"
    ],
    "ceiling_factor": 1.0,
    "non_eu_import_vat_pct": 19,
    "warn_feedback_below": 10,
    "skip_suspiciously_cheap": true,
    "_help_skip": "skip_suspiciously_cheap: on eBay a card under scam_ratio x its used value (gpus[].max_eur, not capped by the budget) is in practice a cooler, box, photo or fake, so it is dropped instead of alerted. Set false to get those alerts with a warning instead.",
    "exclude_title_patterns": [
      "defekt", "kaputt", "bastler", "\\bersatz", "ohne funktion", "for parts", "faulty",
      "not working", "\\bbroken\\b", "\\bsuche\\b", "nur (ovp|karton|verpackung)", "\\bnur (der|die|das|den)\\b",
