  "shops": {
    "_help": "Cypriot computer shops (new cards, a few refurbished). Read every every_minutes in the background, at each shop's robots.txt crawl-delay, with an honest bot user agent. Only cards you can order now are compared with the ceilings. ceiling_factor multiplies gpus[].max_eur for shops only: 1.0 keeps your rule of never paying more than the used value; a new card with warranty may be worth e.g. 1.15. Set a shop to false to stop reading it. needy.shop is not supported (its terms forbid scraping).",
    "enabled": true,
    "every_minutes": 30,
    "ceiling_factor": 1.0,
    "armenius": true,
    "bionic": true,
    "custompc": true,
    "computerg": true
  },
  "business": {
    "_help": "Second buyer: a friend's VAT-registered family business that reclaims the VAT on shop invoices. For shop listings only (a VAT invoice is needed), any card from gpus[] whose shop price falls min_drop_pct or more below the first price the bot saw, with the price without VAT at or under budget_eur, is alerted as [BUSINESS PRICE DROP]. Each cut alerts once; again only after a further 3% drop. Set enabled to false to stop.",
    "enabled": true,
    "name": "the business",
    "vat_pct": 19,
    "budget_eur": 600,
    "min_drop_pct": 10
  },
  "pcs": {
    "_help": "Complete desktop PCs. The bot reads the graphics card, processor and RAM an advert names, prices each at what it costs USED when bought on its own (the tables below), adds rest_eur for the board, PSU, case and SSD, and alerts when the PC costs at most max_price_ratio x that sum (1.05 = up to 5% more than the parts bought one by one; 1.0 = no dearer than the parts; 0.85 = only PCs at least 15% cheaper). The alert says how the price compares, and GREAT DEAL marks PCs at least 16% cheaper than their parts. A PC seen earlier that qualifies only after you loosen these settings alerts once. A part the advert does not name counts as 0, so a vague advert never looks cheap. budget_eur: null = no price cap. A PC only counts with a graphics card from your 12GB+ list (gpus[]), or with a processor worth min_cpu_eur or more plus at least min_ram_gb of RAM (a strong base to add your own card to); smaller cards still add their value to the sum. Sources: the desktop sections of bazaraki and vendora every every_minutes, and (shops: true) the complete PCs of the four shops every shops_every_minutes. For bazaraki adverts whose title leaves parts open the seller's description is read once (at most detail_fetches_per_scan adverts per scan, only above details_min_price).",
    "enabled": true,
    "max_price_ratio": 1.05,
    "budget_eur": null,
    "min_cpu_eur": 60,
    "min_ram_gb": 16,
    "every_minutes": 10,
    "bazaraki_pages": 2,
    "vendora_pages": 2,
    "shops": true,
    "shops_every_minutes": 180,
    "detail_fetches_per_scan": 6,
    "details_min_price": 150,
